hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"27670","Haddathana Sufyan ibn Uyaynah, from Ibn Ishaq, from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-Taymi, he said: I heard Buqayrah, wife of al-Qa'qa' ibn Abi Hadrad, saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, upon the minbar saying: When you hear of an army swallowed up nearby, the Hour has cast its shadow."
"27671","Haddathana Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Razi, he said: Haddathana Salamah ibn al-Fadl, he said: Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to me from Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Ata', from Buqayrah, wife of al-Qa'qa', she said: I was sitting in the bench of the women, and I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, preaching while gesturing with his left hand, saying: O people, when you hear of a swallowing nearby, the Hour has cast its shadow."
